---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Header, Footer } from '../components/ui';
import { challenges } from '../lib/growth-content';
import '../styles/business.css';
---
<Base title="Free Minimal-Pair Listening Activities for Teachers | MinimalPairs" description="Share English and French minimal-pair listening challenges with your class. Ship vs sheep, tu vs tout and more, with audio feedback and no account required for challenges.">
  <Header /><main class="editorial-wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">FOR LANGUAGE TEACHERS</p><h1>A listening warm-up.<br/>One link for your class.</h1>
    <p class="editorial-lede">Can your students hear the difference between ship and sheep, or tu and tout? Choose a free challenge, share its link, and let them listen before they see the words.</p>
    <section><h2>Choose your classroom challenge</h2><div class="editorial-link-grid">{challenges.map(c=><a href={`/challenge/${c.slug}`}><strong>{c.title}</strong><span>{c.language==='en'?'American English':'French'} · Free challenge →</span></a>)}</div><p>The challenges work without a student account. The full practice library is available with a paid membership.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Add a challenge to your class page</h2><p>Copy a link card into your website or learning platform. Students open the free activity on MinimalPairs.</p>{challenges.map(c=><details style="margin:1rem 0"><summary>{c.title}</summary><label style="display:block;margin:.6rem 0">HTML link card<textarea readonly rows="4" style="display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;font:14px/1.5 monospace;padding:12px" aria-label={`HTML link card for ${c.title}`}>{`<a href="https://minimalpairs.co/challenge/${c.slug}?utm_source=partner&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=listening-challenge" style="display:block;padding:20px;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:12px;color:#202520;text-decoration:none"><strong>${c.title}</strong><br>Try a free listening challenge on MinimalPairs →</a>`}</textarea></label><a href={`https://minimalpairs.co/challenge/${c.slug}?utm_source=partner&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=listening-challenge`}>Preview this challenge →</a></details>)}</section>
    <section><h2>A five-minute lesson plan</h2><ol><li><strong>Listen first.</strong> Open a challenge on a shared screen, or send the link for individual headphone practice. Keep the spelling hidden.</li><li><strong>Make a choice.</strong> Students hear two reference words, then a different word in another voice. Ask which reference shares the target sound.</li><li><strong>Hear the answer.</strong> The matching sounds replay after each response. Let students explain what helped them distinguish the sounds.</li><li><strong>Reveal and revisit.</strong> Show the words after listening, then try another round. The aim is to recognize the sound across words and voices.</li></ol></section>
    <section><h2>Find each learner’s next step</h2><p>Use a listening diagnostic for individual follow-up. Students can choose a Short Test or Full Diagnostics, then see their score and a sample from their results.</p><div class="editorial-link-grid"><a href="/diagnostic/en"><strong>English listening diagnostic</strong><span>Choose a test →</span></a><a href="/diagnostic/fr"><strong>French listening diagnostic</strong><span>Choose a test →</span></a></div></section>
    <section><h2>Keep the sound guide handy</h2><p>Use the word audio and IPA to revisit the contrast after the activity.</p><div class="editorial-link-grid"><a href="/english-minimal-pairs"><strong>English sound guides</strong><span>Explore vowel and consonant contrasts →</span></a><a href="/french-minimal-pairs"><strong>French sound guides</strong><span>Explore vowels, nasal vowels and consonants →</span></a></div></section>
  </main><Footer />
</Base>
